00:13:15,140 --> 00:13:18,060
this could lead to a general rise in expectations.

339
00:13:18,060 --> 00:13:19,660
So even though in the short run, it

340
00:13:19,660 --> 00:13:22,740
may appear that I benefit from my reputation

341
00:13:22,740 --> 00:13:24,820
for being a good person, in the long run,

342
00:13:24,820 --> 00:13:27,300
I will have so interfered with the market

343
00:13:27,300 --> 00:13:29,740
that my opportunities will be depressed and limited.

344
00:13:29,740 --> 00:13:33,100
All right, so this would be what a megalomaniac would think.

345
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:35,060
But anyway, that same person says,

346
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:36,700
I'm just one little person here.

347
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:38,660
The world does not revolve around me.

348
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:40,700
So I can just assume that whatever I do

349
00:13:40,700 --> 00:13:44,100
has no effect on general behavior.

350
00:13:44,100 --> 00:13:45,980
So that's what it's like to be single.

351
00:13:45,980 --> 00:13:47,580
On the other hand, suppose that you've

352
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:49,580
been married for 10 years, you have three kids,

353
00:13:49,580 --> 00:13:52,900
and then you're thinking, well, look,

354
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:55,980
I don't need to worry about being mistreated by my spouse

355
00:13:55,980 --> 00:13:58,740
because the market.

356
00:13:58,740 --> 00:14:00,940
There are millions of other people I could be dating.

357
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:03,900
So if my spouse were to give me anything 1%

358
00:14:03,900 --> 00:14:07,060
below my opportunity cost, then this

359
00:14:07,060 --> 00:14:08,560
would lead to immediate dissolution.

360
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:11,460
I'd switch to another person, and problem solved.

361
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:14,620
So once you have put a lot of investment in the relationship,

362
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:17,140
the fact that there's lots of other opportunities

363
00:14:17,140 --> 00:14:18,780
is no longer very much protection.

364
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:21,340
On the other hand, if you were to say, look,

365
00:14:21,340 --> 00:14:23,980
I mean, there'd be no point in me being 1% nicer,

366
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:25,980
because all that would happen was I would then

367
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:27,780
get a million other dating opportunities.

368
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:31,980
So there's no real reason for me to give flowers like an extra

369
00:14:31,980 --> 00:14:34,380
just because of flowers to your spouse.

370
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:36,880
And of course, this is not what people who are married generally

371
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,060
think is going on.

372
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:41,220
Instead, they think, we both have a lot invested here.

373
00:14:41,220 --> 00:14:45,380
So on the one hand, either of us could fall quite short,

374
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:47,340
and still we'd probably stay together.

375
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:50,420
Or on the other hand, one of us could go and improve a lot

376
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:54,900
and would not automatically lead to any better treatments.

377
00:14:54,900 --> 00:14:58,100
And then, well, simple, if I started to say,

378
00:14:58,100 --> 00:15:00,260
I cut back my wasteful spending, would this

379
00:15:00,260 --> 00:15:03,220
lead my spouse to cut back their wasteful spending?

380
00:15:03,220 --> 00:15:07,420
Or maybe they would just gobble up more of the free resources?

381
00:15:07,420 --> 00:15:08,740
What's going to happen here?

382
00:15:08,740 --> 00:15:09,860
And this is true even though there

383
00:15:09,860 --> 00:15:11,320
was one point in your life when you

384
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:12,780
had millions of opportunities.

385
00:15:12,780 --> 00:15:15,020
But once you have been together for quite a while

386
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:16,900
and made some common investments,

387
00:15:16,900 --> 00:15:23,020
then the market no longer is all that relevant.

388
00:15:23,020 --> 00:15:25,460
You say, well, things got extreme enough.

389
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:26,300
Then it would matter.

390
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:29,180
Yeah, so it's not saying the market doesn't matter at all.

391
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:32,820
So your opportunity costs or your outside opportunities

392
00:15:32,820 --> 00:15:34,380
still matter to some degree.

393
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:37,460
But within a big range, they might be totally irrelevant.

394
00:15:37,460 --> 00:15:41,180
And then you sit there saying, well, what am I going to do now?

395
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:44,780
Do I just sit here and listen to my mother-in-law insult me?

396
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:46,340
I mean, if this were a first date

397
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:49,620
and I were being insulted by my date's mother,

398
00:15:49,620 --> 00:15:52,380
I'd probably just decide to move on.

399
00:15:52,380 --> 00:15:53,820
But now I'm at a point in my life

400
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:55,740
where maybe I just need to sit here and shut up

401
00:15:55,740 --> 00:15:57,980
and take the abuse.

402
00:15:57,980 --> 00:16:01,820
OK, nothing to do with me.

403
00:16:01,820 --> 00:16:06,580
TV, movies, this is all my life experience.

404
00:16:06,580 --> 00:16:11,180
Once in a while, someone opens up to me, but not often.

405
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:14,460
One friend who told me stuff.

406
00:16:14,460 --> 00:16:17,460
That's what's going on now.

407
00:16:17,460 --> 00:16:19,260
So game theory tries to analyze situations

408
00:16:19,260 --> 00:16:22,900
where strategy does matter and usually ends up

409
00:16:22,900 --> 00:16:25,460
with answers that are a lot vaguer or foggier

410
00:16:25,460 --> 00:16:27,100
than general equilibrium.

411
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:29,300
But at least a lot of people think game theory is more

412
00:16:29,300 --> 00:16:30,980
realistic.

413
00:16:30,980 --> 00:16:34,540
And there is a line from famous behavioral economist

414
00:16:34,540 --> 00:16:36,900
and now Nobel Prize winner Richard Thaler, which

415
00:16:36,900 --> 00:16:40,620
is I'd rather be vaguely right than clearly wrong.

416
00:16:40,620 --> 00:16:43,140
And this is a motivation behind a lot of game theory

417
00:16:43,140 --> 00:16:46,580
compared to general equilibrium.

418
00:16:46,580 --> 00:16:47,460
So questions?

419
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:48,540
Everyone happy?

420
00:16:48,540 --> 00:16:49,040
Satisfied?

421
00:16:49,040 --> 00:16:49,740
All right, good.

