00:20:06,040 --> 00:20:09,200
And player one gets the first payoff.

4
00:20:09,200 --> 00:20:10,760
Player two gets the second payoff.

5
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:13,440
It's very normal in game theory to just call people player one,

6
00:20:13,440 --> 00:20:15,040
player two, player three.

7
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:17,840
Normally, player one is the person who plays first.

8
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:19,600
Player two is the player who plays second.

9
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:21,400
Player three is the player who plays third.

10
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:25,280
So it's very simple.

11
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:26,240
OK.

12
00:20:26,240 --> 00:20:30,400
All right, so you could have your career game tree.

