363
01:37:16,680 --> 01:37:18,520
How do I accomplish this?

364
01:37:18,520 --> 01:37:21,040
So, I can stay up all night playing video games.

365
01:37:21,040 --> 01:37:24,960
But, anyway, so that's a game example I know of a hard bargainer.

366
01:37:24,960 --> 01:37:27,440
Here's the thing, when people bargain hard,

367
01:37:27,440 --> 01:37:32,280
there are advantages like you can get more for yourself if a deal still occurs.

368
01:37:32,280 --> 01:37:35,640
However, there's also the risk that you kill the deal.

369
01:37:35,640 --> 01:37:38,080
And those are the trade-offs.

370
01:37:38,080 --> 01:37:40,120
On the other end, if you're a soft bargainer,

371
01:37:40,120 --> 01:37:44,240
then you can almost always get to a deal,

372
01:37:44,240 --> 01:37:47,280
although the deals that you have will be relatively unfavorable.

373
01:37:47,280 --> 01:37:51,640
Okay. All right. Now, which strategy works better in equilibrium?

374
01:37:51,640 --> 01:37:54,200
And the mixed strategy and national equilibrium answer is neither.

375
01:37:54,200 --> 01:37:56,320
In equilibrium, they must be equally profitable.

376
01:37:56,320 --> 01:37:59,760
So, we need to get to probability such that

377
01:37:59,760 --> 01:38:02,800
the extra benefits that you get from

378
01:38:02,800 --> 01:38:08,040
bargaining hard are exactly balanced by the reduced probability that you get to a deal at all.

379
01:38:08,040 --> 01:38:10,000
On the other hand, for the soft bargainers,

380
01:38:10,000 --> 01:38:13,400
you get to a world where the loss and benefits that you could get from

381
01:38:13,400 --> 01:38:19,480
bargaining harder are exactly compensated by the extra deals that you get to make.

382
01:38:19,480 --> 01:38:23,720
So, that is the idea.

383
01:38:23,720 --> 01:38:28,880
All right. Now, let's see.

384
01:38:28,880 --> 01:38:32,800
So, questions about that? Questions? All right.

385
01:38:32,800 --> 01:38:34,640
Now, I would say in general,

386
01:38:34,640 --> 01:38:37,760
a rule is that the more people understand the world,

387
01:38:37,760 --> 01:38:41,680
I mean, my view is that people who understand the world are generally softer bargainers,

388
01:38:41,680 --> 01:38:46,960
and that hard bargainers have the naive view of the more I ask for,

389
01:38:46,960 --> 01:38:49,360
the more I get, which is often true.

390
01:38:49,360 --> 01:38:52,960
But they're forgetting the downside risk of alienating people,

391
01:38:52,960 --> 01:38:55,680
either preventing a deal or there's actually like the really bad thing,

392
01:38:55,680 --> 01:38:57,200
like you suppose you go to your boss and you say,

