244
01:73:20,080 --> 01:73:21,280
All right?

245
01:73:21,280 --> 01:73:24,400
So people use it to understand public goods and externalities.

246
01:73:24,400 --> 01:73:27,520
Why is it that it's so hard to voluntarily supply public good?

247
01:73:27,520 --> 01:73:31,120
Well, there's a Prisoner's Dilemma story.

248
01:73:31,120 --> 01:73:35,240
So what happens to you if you voluntarily contribute to the public good and it still

249
01:73:35,240 --> 01:73:38,280
doesn't get produced?

250
01:73:38,280 --> 01:73:39,560
You wasted your time.

251
01:73:39,560 --> 01:73:44,000
What happens if you voluntarily contribute to a public good and it does get produced?

252
01:73:44,000 --> 01:73:46,600
You wasted your time because it would have happened without you.

253
01:73:46,600 --> 01:73:47,600
All right?

254
01:73:47,600 --> 01:73:50,320
So that's, you know, a standard story about public goods and externalities.

255
01:73:50,320 --> 01:73:53,920
And again, like, isn't it possible that what you do makes a difference?

256
01:73:53,920 --> 01:73:56,800
Yeah, if you like, your contribution is the crucial one.

