But nevertheless, it is basically the Kickstarter model.

101
01:86:11,400 --> 01:86:16,400
And I prefer the view that Alex was the original, because it was the original source.

102
01:86:16,400 --> 01:86:21,400
I could go proof of this, but it just seems like whenever a good idea gets out there and

103
01:86:21,400 --> 01:86:25,400
the first person I heard it from was one of my friends, that my friend deserves credit.

104
01:86:25,400 --> 01:86:26,400
All right.

105
01:86:26,400 --> 01:86:29,400
Anyway, like I said, there's a lot of experimental literature on the prison-office lemma.

106
01:86:29,400 --> 01:86:34,400
Extreme prediction very rarely borne out, because people do cooperate sometimes, even

107
01:86:34,400 --> 01:86:36,400
when the defection is strictly dominant.

108
01:86:36,400 --> 01:86:40,400
But people do leave money on the table, and there's a bunch of standard ways to reduce

109
01:86:40,400 --> 01:86:46,400
cooperation, things like make it more anonymous, reduce the level of contact between the people.

110
01:86:46,400 --> 01:86:49,400
I've heard of versions where you actually get people who have personal animosity playing

111
01:86:49,400 --> 01:86:50,400
against each other.

112
01:86:50,400 --> 01:86:54,400
So I've heard of a version where they actually had Israeli students play Palestinian students

113
01:86:54,400 --> 01:86:55,400
remotely.

114
01:86:55,400 --> 01:87:00,400
So you start with people who have a negative view of the other group, and yeah, as you

115
01:87:00,400 --> 01:87:02,400
might guess, you get less cooperation.

116
01:87:02,400 --> 01:87:05,400
Of course, flip side is there's some standard ways to raise cooperation.

117
01:87:05,400 --> 01:87:08,400
So if you want to get people to cooperate more, tell them to take out their phones and

118
01:87:08,400 --> 01:87:10,400
share pictures of their family members.

119
01:87:10,400 --> 01:87:14,400
And then you humanize your opponent, and this predictably does raise cooperation.

120
01:87:14,400 --> 01:87:15,400
All right.

121
01:87:15,400 --> 01:87:16,400
Now last.

122
01:87:16,400 --> 01:87:19,400
So there's no experiment, as far as I know, that's ever been done that's had people

123
01:87:19,400 --> 01:87:21,400
play for, say, a year.

124
01:87:21,400 --> 01:87:24,400
So it's common for experimenters to say, there's never been an experiment shown that

125
01:87:24,400 --> 01:87:25,400
cooperation goes to zero.

126
01:87:25,400 --> 01:87:28,400
Yeah, well, you've also never run an experiment lasting for more than a few days.

127
01:87:28,400 --> 01:87:33,400
So don't act like it's not that impressive to say there is no such experiment.

128
01:87:33,400 --> 01:87:37,400
When someone says no experiment shows this, worth asking, well, what experiment's been

